/-!
# Cover calculus for prime-to-ell alterations

Source: ILO, Travaux de Gabber, Exposé II 1.2.5--1.2.8, 2.2.4 and 2.3.1,
printed pp. 25--28 (blueprint: lem-per-alteration-cover-calculus).

Reduced dominant parts are characterized by a closed immersion with its exact image.
This determines the reduced induced subscheme uniquely, including its maps, rather than
choosing an unspecified base-change map. The base-change functor below uses this same
characterization and includes compatibility with both projections.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u w w' w''

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeToEllAlteration

/-- Cover calculus for `alt/S`. Source: ILO II 1.2.5--1.2.8, 2.2.4 and 2.3.1, pp. 25--28
(blueprint: lem-per-alteration-cover-calculus).

Proof:
1. Unpack `Alt`. Finite type over a Noetherian base gives Noetherian objects
   (`lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-over-noetherian`). The generic-fibre finiteness criterion
   (`lem-per-generic-fibre-finiteness-criterion`) shows that arrows preserve generic points
   and have finite generic residue extensions; they are also of finite type.
2. Form the ordinary fibre product and retain the reduced union of its components
   dominating the common target. The coreflection `lem-per-dominant-part-coreflection`
   gives its universal property in `Alt`. Its generic fibres remain finite, by the tensor
   product description of finite algebras and `lem-sfb-finite-type-composition-base-change`.
3. Pull back the two generating kinds. Étale base change agrees with ordinary base change;
   proper surjections remain proper surjective after dominant reduction. Apply
   `lem-per-prime-to-ell-residue-base-change` to retain a good residue degree. Use
   `lem-weil-pbc-etale-covering-base-change`, `lem-weil-pbc-proper-base-change` and
   `lem-weil-pbc-surjective-base-change`.
4. Extract finite étale generators using
   `lem-per-prime-to-ell-decomposed-etale-finite-subcover`. Close finite generators and
   isomorphisms under finite rooted trees. Grafting gives composition stability; pulling
   back one vertex at a time gives base-change stability. Every tree has finitely many leaves.
5. This precoverage generates `topology`: each original generator contains a finite one,
   and every tree covers by local character. Apply
   `lem-per-generated-precoverage-covering-sieve` to get a finite family in every covering
   sieve; factor its arrows through the original family to obtain a refinement.
6. The sieve axioms give composition, coarsening, and refinement by covering families.
   The pullback of a generated sieve is generated by the categorical fibre products.
   A dependent sum of finite index sets is finite.
7. For a dominant finite-type map of integral Noetherian bases, take the reduced dominant
   part of each ordinary base change. Its generic fibre is finite. The coreflection gives
   functoriality and comparison of iterated products: a reduced test scheme dominant over
   the new integral base is also maximally dominant over the old base. This needs no flatness.
8. The functor sends each generator to a generator by the same étale comparison, proper
   surjectivity and residue-degree argument of step 3. Send a finite generator-tree
   refinement to such a tree over the new base, then coarsen to the image family.
9. For integral objects, a proper surjective map of finite prime-to-ell generic degree is
   a singleton generator. A proper birational map has generic degree one.
10. Finite affine open covers are decomposed étale generators, with residue degree one.
    Their members are objects by `lem-weil-pbc-open-immersion-etale` and
    `lem-weil-pbc-qc-open-immersion-finite-type`. The empty cover is included.
11. There are finitely many components (`lem-weil-pbc-noetherian-finite-components`). Give
    them their reduced closed structures (`lem-weil-pbc-reduced-induced-closed-subscheme`).
    Their disjoint union is finite over the object, hence proper, surjective and of generic
    degree one (`lem-weil-pbc-closed-immersion-finite`, `lem-weil-pbc-finite-proper` and
    `lem-weil-pbc-scheme-coproduct-family`). Its summand open cover, followed by composition,
    gives the component cover. For the empty object use the empty family. -/
theorem alteration_cover_calculus (S : Scheme.{u}) [IsNoetherian S]
    (ell : ℕ) [Fact ell.Prime] :
    (∀ (T : Alt S) (I : Type w) [Finite I] (U : I → Alt S)
      (f : ∀ i, U i ⟶ T) (J : I → Type w') [∀ i, Finite (J i)]
      (V : ∀ i, J i → Alt S) (g : ∀ i j, V i j ⟶ U i),
      IsCoveringFamily ell U f → (∀ i, IsCoveringFamily ell (V i) (g i)) →
      IsCoveringFamily ell (fun ij : Sigma J ↦ V ij.1 ij.2)
        (fun ij ↦ g ij.1 ij.2 ≫ f ij.1)) ∧
    (∀ (T : Alt S) (I : Type w) (U : I → Alt S) (f : ∀ i, U i ⟶ T)
      (J : I → Type w') (V : ∀ i, J i → Alt S) (g : ∀ i j, V i j ⟶ U i)
      (K : Type w'') (W : K → Alt S) (h : ∀ k, W k ⟶ T),
      IsCoveringFamily ell U f → (∀ i, IsCoveringFamily ell (V i) (g i)) →
      Refines (fun ij : Sigma J ↦ V ij.1 ij.2) (fun ij ↦ g ij.1 ij.2 ≫ f ij.1) W h →
      IsCoveringFamily ell W h) ∧
    (∀ (T : Alt S) (R : Sieve T), R ∈ topology S ell T →
      ∃ (n : ℕ) (U : Fin n → Alt S) (f : ∀ i, U i ⟶ T),
        IsCoveringFamily ell U f ∧ ∀ i, R (f i)) ∧
    (∀ (T X Y : Alt S) (f : X ⟶ T) (g : Y ⟶ T),
      ∃ (P : Alt S) (p : P ⟶ X) (q : P ⟶ Y)
        (j : P.obj.left ⟶ pullback f.hom.left g.hom.left),
        IsPullback p q f g ∧ IsClosedImmersion j ∧
        j ≫ pullback.fst f.hom.left g.hom.left = p.hom.left ∧
        j ≫ pullback.snd f.hom.left g.hom.left = q.hom.left ∧
        Set.range j = {z | ∃ c ∈ irreducibleComponents
          (pullback f.hom.left g.hom.left : Scheme.{u}), z ∈ c ∧
          closure ((pullback.fst f.hom.left g.hom.left ≫ f.hom.left) '' c) ∈
            irreducibleComponents T.obj.left}) ∧
    (∀ (T Y : Alt S) (g : Y ⟶ T) (I : Type w) (U : I → Alt S)
      (f : ∀ i, U i ⟶ T) (P : I → Alt S) (p : ∀ i, P i ⟶ U i)
      (q : ∀ i, P i ⟶ Y),
      (∀ i, IsPullback (p i) (q i) (f i) g) → IsCoveringFamily ell U f →
      IsCoveringFamily ell P q) ∧
    (∀ (S' : Scheme.{u}) [IsIntegral S] [IsIntegral S'] [IsNoetherian S']
      (a : S' ⟶ S) [IsDominant a] [LocallyOfFiniteType a] [QuasiCompact a],
      ∃ (F : Alt S ⥤ Alt S')
        (j : ∀ X : Alt S, (F.obj X).obj.left ⟶ pullback X.obj.hom a),
        (∀ X, IsClosedImmersion (j X) ∧
          j X ≫ pullback.snd X.obj.hom a = (F.obj X).obj.hom ∧
          Set.range (j X) = {z | ∃ c ∈ irreducibleComponents
            (pullback X.obj.hom a : Scheme.{u}),
            z ∈ c ∧ Dense (pullback.snd X.obj.hom a '' c)}) ∧
        (∀ (X Y : Alt S) (f : X ⟶ Y),
          (F.map f).hom.left ≫ j Y ≫ pullback.fst Y.obj.hom a =
            j X ≫ pullback.fst X.obj.hom a ≫ f.hom.left) ∧
        (∀ (T : Alt S) (I : Type w) (U : I → Alt S) (f : ∀ i, U i ⟶ T),
          IsCoveringFamily ell U f →
          IsCoveringFamily ell (fun i ↦ F.obj (U i)) (fun i ↦ F.map (f i)))) ∧
    (∀ (T U : Alt S) [IsIntegral T.obj.left] [IsIntegral U.obj.left]
      (f : U ⟶ T), IsProper f.hom.left → Surjective f.hom.left →
      (∀ x : U.obj.left, closure ({x} : Set U.obj.left) ∈
        irreducibleComponents U.obj.left →
        (f.hom.left.residueFieldMap x).hom.Finite ∧
          Nat.Coprime (f.hom.left.residueDegree x) ell) →
      IsCoveringFamily ell (fun _ : Fin 1 ↦ U) (fun _ ↦ f)) ∧
    (∀ (T U : Alt S) [IsIntegral T.obj.left] [IsIntegral U.obj.left]
      (f : U ⟶ T), IsProper f.hom.left →
      (∃ V : T.obj.left.Opens, Dense (V : Set T.obj.left) ∧ IsIso (f.hom.left ∣_ V)) →
      IsCoveringFamily ell (fun _ : Fin 1 ↦ U) (fun _ ↦ f)) ∧
    (∀ (T : Alt S) (I : Type w) [Finite I] (U : I → Alt S)
      (f : ∀ i, U i ⟶ T),
      (∀ i, IsAffine (U i).obj.left ∧ IsOpenImmersion (f i).hom.left) →
      (∀ t : T.obj.left, ∃ (i : I) (x : (U i).obj.left), (f i).hom.left x = t) →
      IsCoveringFamily ell U f) ∧
    (∀ T : Alt S, ∃ (n : ℕ) (U : Fin n → Alt S) (f : ∀ i, U i ⟶ T)
      (e : Fin n ≃ {c : Set T.obj.left // c ∈ irreducibleComponents T.obj.left}),
      (∀ i, IsClosedImmersion (f i).hom.left ∧ Set.range (f i).hom.left = (e i).1) ∧
      IsCoveringFamily ell U f) ∧
    (∀ T : Alt S, IsReduced T.obj.left ∧ LocallyOfFiniteType T.obj.hom ∧
      QuasiCompact T.obj.hom ∧
      ∀ t : T.obj.left, closure ({t} : Set T.obj.left) ∈ irreducibleComponents T.obj.left →
        closure ({T.obj.hom t} : Set S) ∈ irreducibleComponents S ∧
          (T.obj.hom.residueFieldMap t).hom.Finite) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeToEllAlteration
